  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Unseasonably warm temperatures continue\nacross today and over the weekend with high temperatures reaching\nnear record as the high pressure system over the southwest\ncontinue strengthen. Warmest temperatures expected Saturday and\nSunday as highs reach into the upper 80s with a few 90 degrees\nexpected in northern Nevada. By the start of next week,\ntemperatures will slightly cool down but remain above normal for\nthis time of year with parts of northern Nevada still hovering\nnear record temperatures in the 80s, while central Nevada cools\ninto the upper 70s to low 80s. This temperatures trend is expected\nto last all through Thursday with northern Nevada staying well\nabove normal in the 80s. By the end of next week, temperatures\nstart to see a cooling trend dropping back into the 70s over\nnorthern Nevada with a few spots remaining in the low 80s. Winds\nwill be generally light below 10 mph with a few peak gusts in the\nafternoons up to 15-20 mph.",
